## 6. Security, Compliance & Data Protection

### 6.1 Authentication & Authorization
- Server-side token/session verification on all protected endpoints.
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) enforced at the database or middleware layer.

### 6.2 Data Validation & Sanitization
- All client inputs validated on server using schema validation libraries.
- Strict SQL injection prevention via parameterized ORM queries.
- XSS prevention via automatic template escaping.

### 6.3 Secrets & Environment Security
- Zero secrets committed to source control.
- All credentials injected via system environment variables.

